20	breakpoint.yml:preflight	breakpoint.yml is in the frozen set hashed by .ci/breakpoint/MANIFEST.sha256 (workflow/breakpoint.yml) and must stay byte-identical in every repository that vendors breakpoint; check-breakpoint-drift.sh cmp's the live copy against the template, so a console-only profiler step would fail that gate. The session job is also runner-agnostic by design (runs-on is the dispatch input, chosen per session), so there is no single runner-label to arm the HOST_LEAK check with.
21	breakpoint.yml:session	breakpoint.yml is in the frozen set hashed by .ci/breakpoint/MANIFEST.sha256 (workflow/breakpoint.yml) and must stay byte-identical in every repository that vendors breakpoint; check-breakpoint-drift.sh cmp's the live copy against the template, so a console-only profiler step would fail that gate. The session job is also runner-agnostic by design (runs-on is the dispatch input, chosen per session), so there is no single runner-label to arm the HOST_LEAK check with.
24	profiler-probe.yml:facts-latest	these are the profiler probe's own experiment arms and adding a direct profiler step would destroy the measurement. facts-slim/facts-latest run the sampler in --probe form only, on purpose: they answer what a job inside the ubuntu-slim container can read from /sys/fs/cgroup, and a second sampler in the same job would contend with the one being measured. post-nested-slim/post-nested-latest are the TREATMENT arm of the nesting question (does a JavaScript action's post: hook fire when nested inside a composite?); giving them a direct uses: as well would make a panel appear whether or not nesting works, which is precisely the thing the probe exists to distinguish.
25	profiler-probe.yml:facts-slim	these are the profiler probe's own experiment arms and adding a direct profiler step would destroy the measurement. facts-slim/facts-latest run the sampler in --probe form only, on purpose: they answer what a job inside the ubuntu-slim container can read from /sys/fs/cgroup, and a second sampler in the same job would contend with the one being measured. post-nested-slim/post-nested-latest are the TREATMENT arm of the nesting question (does a JavaScript action's post: hook fire when nested inside a composite?); giving them a direct uses: as well would make a panel appear whether or not nesting works, which is precisely the thing the probe exists to distinguish.
26	profiler-probe.yml:post-nested-latest	these are the profiler probe's own experiment arms and adding a direct profiler step would destroy the measurement. facts-slim/facts-latest run the sampler in --probe form only, on purpose: they answer what a job inside the ubuntu-slim container can read from /sys/fs/cgroup, and a second sampler in the same job would contend with the one being measured. post-nested-slim/post-nested-latest are the TREATMENT arm of the nesting question (does a JavaScript action's post: hook fire when nested inside a composite?); giving them a direct uses: as well would make a panel appear whether or not nesting works, which is precisely the thing the probe exists to distinguish.
27	profiler-probe.yml:post-nested-slim	these are the profiler probe's own experiment arms and adding a direct profiler step would destroy the measurement. facts-slim/facts-latest run the sampler in --probe form only, on purpose: they answer what a job inside the ubuntu-slim container can read from /sys/fs/cgroup, and a second sampler in the same job would contend with the one being measured. post-nested-slim/post-nested-latest are the TREATMENT arm of the nesting question (does a JavaScript action's post: hook fire when nested inside a composite?); giving them a direct uses: as well would make a panel appear whether or not nesting works, which is precisely the thing the probe exists to distinguish.
32	autopilot.yml:finish	rollout ledger for the runner profiler, which landed 2026-08-05 with one live job (profiler-probe.yml:post-direct-latest) and 90 jobs still unwired. Enumerated rather than waived so the gate is BLOCKING for every job added from today on, and so the burn-down is a visible diff instead of a habit: each line is deleted by the commit that adds the profiler step to that job, and the gate rejects the line the moment the job is covered, so a forgotten deletion is a build failure rather than dead weight. Phase 1 landed 2026-08-08 and burned 25 of these lines at once: profiler-probe.yml run 31252148469 proved on real runners that a JavaScript action's post: hook DOES fire from inside a composite, so one uses: in .github/actions/setup-workspace plus one verified wrapper in the gate covered every job that already calls it. What remains here is the jobs that do NOT call setup-workspace -- they set up their own toolchain, or run nothing that needs node -- and each of those still needs its own edit.
